   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Viktor Petrovich, are you alive?' Notice the word order: 'Viktor' comes first, and 'living' finishes the sentence.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "А?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Huh?' Notice the word order: 'and' comes first, and 'and' finishes the sentence.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "elena",
   "t": "Ой, вы простите меня.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Oh, please forgive me.' Here 'oh' sets up the idea, while 'me' comes at the end for emphasis.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "elena",
   "t": "Ради бога, простите.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'For God's sake, forgive me.' Listen for the word meaning 'God' right alongside 'excuse me' in this line.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "elena",
   "t": "Я вас просто не заметила.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I just didn't see you.' In Russian, 'I' leads into 'to notice' in a very natural everyday phrasing.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Так вы расправляетесь с конкурентами.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'So this is how you deal with the competition.' A compact expression built around 'you' and 'rival'. Then Elena replies.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "elena",
   "t": "Дайте, я вас приподниму.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Here, let me help you up.' Elena puts 'give' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'I'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "elena",
   "t": "Поедем в больницу.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We will go to the hospital.' Elena starts with 'will be off' and pairs it with 'the hospital' to make the point clear.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Мне больно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'It hurts.' The first content word means 'to me', and 'it hurts' rounds out the thought. And Elena jumps in.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "elena",
   "t": "Надо ехать к врачу.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We need to go to the doctor.' The key word here means 'it is necessary', which Elena combines with 'to drive'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Ладно, поехали.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'All right, let's go.' Listen for the word meaning 'here we go' right alongside 'here we go' in this line.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "elena",
   "t": "Осторожно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
